    Bug 1995024 - Part 3: Integrate NTLM support into the EWS client. r=jtracey


    This commit integrates the stand-alone NTLM implementation introduced in part 2
    into the EWS client and its authentication management infrastructure. I went
    back and forth quite a lot regarding the best way to integrate this flow,
    considering how it differs from the other supported authentication flows which,
    from the perspective of the EWS client, are a single step (i.e. generate a token
    to include in the `Authorization` header).

    This implementation comes with a few caveats which I believe are only best fixed
    by reworking some of the client architecture and how it integrates with the
    incoming server architecture, which I'll be looking at next. In the meantime,
    this limitation shouldn't block this stack since none of this support is exposed
    to the user.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D270713

